Smithay 0.7 calls SessionLockHandler::unlock after invalid_unlock from an
unconfirmed lock. Wisp intercepts these requests by resource identity and
confirmation state before forwarding to Smithay; the global is off by default.
XWayland not integrated.

User-reported manual validation (later): swaylock locked and unlocked in a
nested Wisp window; swaylock and Noctalia lock both worked on a real VT.
The user additionally reported no desktop flash during the real-VT lock:
the desktop disappeared, the correct password was entered, and unlock
restored the desktop. The user also tried wrong passwords twice: swaylock
reported `pam_authenticate failed: invalid credentials`, and the lock stayed
in place until the correct password. VT-away/return, hotplug and
locker-disconnect recovery were not separately reported. This
supports locker compatibility, not a complete security-boundary claim.
